  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya, Rwanda. The main objective of the collaboration is  to increase organisational effectiveness and strengthen capacity of partners and participants in order to achieve lasting and quality care of Orphans and Vulnerable Children (OVC) within communities in Kisumu, Kenya and Kigali, Rwanda. 

The partnership will adopt a systems-based approach to civil society organizations capacity building using to identify, analyze and fill the capacity gaps of the collaborating organizations and other stakeholder civil society organizations (CSOs) in what is believed are the key competences. These range from governance structures of CSOs, stakeholder involvement, project management, financial resource management, human resource management, networking and advocacy, technicalcapacity in various OVC priority areas, to knowledge management, monitoring and evaluation, and project sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
